You're only partly off... metal can both corrode and rust.  Leather
can both rot and burn.  For instance, after meeting up with a brown
pudding and rust monster in short order the other day, I had a
corroded throroughly rusted +1 long sword.  A confused scroll of
enchant weapon fixes all damage, and makes the item damageproof.  When
wishing for an item, it is perfectly ok to wish for a fixed item,
rather than rustproof, fireproof, rotproof, etc.  These adjectives are
synonymous when wishing, and fixed is the shortest!

As a side note, the only item that will actually say fixed (as opposed
to rustproof, ect.) when identitied is a crysknife.

